# Atlas pipeline outputs
# `data/*` rather than `data/`: git will not descend into an excluded directory, so a negation
# below an excluded parent has no effect. Ignoring the *contents* leaves the exceptions usable.
data/*
!data/store/
data/store/*
!data/store/catalog-metadata.json
!data/store/INVENTORY.json
# The published artifacts (data/store/artifacts/) and the held-out validation results
# (data/validation/) live in the public GCS data store, not in git (data store design 2026-10-17,
# #468). data/releases/<release>.json lists every object with its bytes and sha256, and
# scripts/fetch_data.py fetches and verifies them into this git-ignored tree. They left tracking on
# 2026-10-17; history was not rewritten. The fits that produced the artifacts are pickles and stay
# local (design §8).
!data/releases/
# The harvested AFND population table is committed, unlike other fetched sources. The rule is
# cost, not principle: MAP is one HTTP request and stays fetched-by-script, but this is 1,825
# requests and about two hours. A pod re-scraping it spent 1.7 billed hours before fitting
# anything. 436 KB is a cheap way to never do that again; `scripts/fetch_afnd.py` still
# regenerates it, and the page cache stays local.
!data/raw/
data/raw/*
!data/raw/afnd_populations.tsv
# Small, immutable public-source snapshots that define the v1 curated candidate set. CPIC marks
# its curated content CC0; SOURCE.json records the exact queries, hashes, release and terms check.
!data/sources/
data/sources/*
!data/sources/cpic/
data/sources/cpic/*
!data/sources/cpic/v1.60.0/
!data/sources/curated/
data/sources/curated/*
!data/sources/curated/manual_candidates.tsv
!data/sources/curated/SOURCE.json
# The reviewed variant-normalization registry (design 2026-09-10 §5) is hand-authored and
# reviewed, unlike the rest of the built P0 registry, so it is committed like
# catalog-metadata.json above rather than treated as build output.
!data/registry/
data/registry/*
!data/registry/variant_normalization.tsv
!data/registry/curated-v1-candidate.1/
# Bucket staging tree for the public Atlas web data (design 2026-10-07 §C.1.3): the runbook's default
# --out for `encode_atlas_web.py --with-downloads`. `data/*` already ignores it; this line says so.
data/atlas-web/
*.pkl

